# Cloud Agent LocalTerra

**Cloud Agent VMs can run LocalTerra** via Docker. Do **not** report `SKIP (no LocalTerra in agent VM)` without provisioning first.

## Wrong probes (false negatives)

- `docker compose ps` / `docker info` **without** `sg docker` → permission denied on Cloud VMs even when the stack is up.
- Host `curl http://127.0.0.1:1317` may hang; use `scripts/lib/localterra-host-curl.sh` helpers or `make wait-localterra`.

## Correct probe

```bash
make has-localterra          # exit 0 = chain up
make status                  # uses sg docker fallback on Cloud VMs
```

## Provision full stack (first time ~10–15 min)

```bash
make setup-cloud-localterra
```

Writes `frontend-dapp/.env.local`, starts indexer (tmux `indexer-dev`). Then `make dev` for the frontend.

## Postgres-only is not “no LocalTerra”

`make setup-indexer-postgres` is for **indexer integration tests only**. For swap/E2E/frontend chain work, use `make setup-cloud-localterra`.

## Docker in non-login shells

```bash
sg docker -c 'docker compose ps'
```

Or start dockerd: see `AGENTS.md` § Docker daemon.
